# id: M28-mark-coverage-grows-after-handover
# covering-test: TestPersistBeforeReplyOracleReportsNothing
# package: ./sim/hunt/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 300
# power-floor: 140
# power-ceiling: 10
# power-measured: 297 of 300, first at seed 0, under current at commit A5-close; was 253 of 300, first at seed 0, at commit 1e2721a+A5-open
# mutates: a mark is reused after the driver has already started writing it, so its coverage grows and the acknowledgement means less than the messages gated on it require. BOTH defences are removed, because either alone prevents it: raft freezing coverage at handover, and the driver refusing to acknowledge a mark whose writes are not all durable. Removing one gives 0 of 300; removing both gives 257 of 300
# re-anchored: 2026-08-30, after `patch-rot-kind` reported STRUCTURAL. Hunk 2's target moved when
#   d276962 rewrote the durability cross-check below it; BOTH mutation sites are intact, so the
#   class still exists and the patch is regenerated rather than the class re-decided. Hunk 1 at
#   -U15 so it opens on `func (r *Raft) dirty()`; hunk 2 at -U2 because 46 unbroken comment lines
#   sit between the site and the next code line, and widening would only anchor on more prose.
#   The mutation is unchanged and proved so: the mutated tree this patch produces is byte-identical
#   to the one the old patch's hunk 1 plus hunk 2's recorded edit produce.
diff --git a/raft/raft.go b/raft/raft.go
--- a/raft/raft.go
+++ b/raft/raft.go
@@ -2844,31 +2844,31 @@ func (r *Raft) sendGatedOn(mark, snapMark PersistMark, m Message) {
 // mutation of persistent state, so a mark exists to gate against.
 func (r *Raft) dirty() {
 	// # A mark's coverage is frozen at handover
 	//
 	// Reusing a mark that has already been handed over lets its coverage grow
 	// after the driver started writing it, so the acknowledgement means strictly
 	// less than the messages gated on that mark require: the driver reports the
 	// first batch durable, raft releases an append response attesting to the
 	// second, and a follower acks index N with N-1 on disk. That was the whole
 	// residue of BUG-005 once the oracle stopped reading the engine's visible
 	// state and started reading what was actually durable.
 	//
 	// It is also a liveness hazard on its own. Under a steady stream of appends
 	// a reused mark never stops growing, so it never becomes fully durable, and
 	// every message gated on it waits forever behind a convoy.
-	if r.dirtyMark == 0 || r.markHandedOff {
+	if r.dirtyMark == 0 {
 		r.nextMark++
 		r.dirtyMark = r.nextMark
 		r.markHandedOff = false
 	}
 }
 
 func (r *Raft) setVote(v NodeID) {
 	if r.vote != v {
 		r.vote = v
 		r.hardStateDirty = true
 		r.dirty()
 	}
 }
 
 func (r *Raft) setTermAndVote(t Term, v NodeID) {
